result.suggestedFix:
Make 'Erase All Data' sync-aware (purge remotely before wiping local) and scope the wipe to app-data keys. (A) sync.ts — add an exported best-effort remote purge:
export async function wipeRemoteAll() {
  const pb = getClient(); if (!isSignedIn()) return;
  const userId = pb.authStore.record!.id; const now = nowIso();
  for (const key of ['tasks','goals'] as const) {
    const rows = await pb.collection(bindings[key].collection).getFullList();
    for (const row of rows) {
      try { await pb.collection('sync_deletions').create({ appId: row.appId, entity: key, deletedAt: now, user: userId }); } catch {}
      try { await pb.collection(bindings[key].collection).delete(row.id); } catch {}
    }
  }
  for (const key of ['snapshots','memories','patterns'] as const) {
    const rows = await pb.collection(bindings[key].collection).getFullList();
    for (const row of rows) { try { await pb.collection(bindings[key].collection).delete(row.id); } catch {} }
  }
  try { const s = await pb.collection('settings').getFullList({ filter: `appId = "preferences"` }); for (const row of s) { try { await pb.collection('settings').delete(row.id); } catch {} } } catch {}
}
(B) useStore.clearAllData — purge remotely BEFORE clearing local (order matters: clearing first then running a full syncNow would re-push local rows because the push step recreates any 'missing' remote record):
clearAllData: async () => {
  try { if (isSignedIn()) await wipeRemoteAll(); } catch { /* offline: local erase still proceeds; sync is best-effort */ }
  set({ tasks: [], history: [], goals: [], aiMemory: [], learnedPatterns: [], lastSyncAt: new Date().toISOString() });
  db.clearAll();
},
(C) db.ts clearAll — enumerate app-data keys explicitly so the device-scoped secret survives:
clearAll: () => {
  [STORAGE_KEYS.tasks, STORAGE_KEYS.goals, STORAGE_KEYS.history, STORAGE_KEYS.aiMemory, STORAGE_KEYS.learnedPatterns, STORAGE_KEYS.preferences, STORAGE_KEYS.syncDeletions]
    .forEach((k) => { if (typeof window !== 'undefined') localStorage.removeItem(k); });
},
This deletes the remote rows so the next pull has nothing to resurrect and preserves the StepFun key per the UI promise. Residual (inherent to best-effort sync): if the device is offline when erase is invoked, wipeRemoteAll rejects and only the local wipe happens, so data resurrects once back online; and snapshots/memories/patterns have no tombstone pipeline, so OTHER devices still holding them could re-push on their next sync. To close both, persist a 'mindsync_wiped_at' marker and have syncCollection skip remote rows whose updatedAt <= wipedAt when there is no local record, and extend the deletion queue to cover those entities.

Persist the import through the db layer inside importData so localStorage (and therefore sync) sees it. Minimal merge-preserving version, replacing useStore.ts:432-444: 

importData: (jsonData) => {
  try {
    const data = JSON.parse(jsonData);
    if (data.tasks && data.history && data.goals) {
      (data.tasks as Task[]).forEach(t => db.saveTask(t));      // db stamps updatedAt when absent -> LWW-safe
      (data.goals as Goal[]).forEach(g => db.saveGoal(g));
      (data.history as DailySnapshot[]).forEach(h => db.saveSnapshot(h)); // keys by date (per-day merge)
      set({ tasks: db.getTasks(), goals: db.getGoals(), history: db.getHistory() });
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  } catch (e) { console.error('Import failed:', e); return false; }
},

Notes for the fix: (a) this is an upsert/merge by id — rows in localStorage but absent from the file survive; if restore semantics are wanted, add wholesale-replace helpers to db.ts (e.g. replaceTasks/replaceGoals/replaceHistory that write the storage keys directly, without enqueueing deletion tombstones — an import is a restore, not a delete) and call those before re-setting state. (b) db.saveTask's stampUpdatedAt preserves absent-only stamping, so imported rows without updatedAt receive 'now' and win/push on the next syncNow — the intended syncable behavior. (c) Optionally extend the import validation to also accept aiMemory/learnedPatterns via db.addAiMemory/db.addLearnedPattern for parity, though exportData currently emits only tasks/history/goals. (d) Add a smoke-test assertion that after importData, localStorage keys mindsync_tasks/mindsync_goals/mindsync_history contain the imported rows — the existing sync-smoke-test.ts never covers import.
